1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,674
A young woman by a dark road, waiting for

2
00:00:02,684 --> 00:00:03,153
a ride.

3
00:00:03,383 --> 00:00:05,273
This is Reder Road, in Griffith.

4
00:00:05,823 --> 00:00:07,824
It once ran a few miles through the woods

5
00:00:07,834 --> 00:00:08,908
toward Merrillville.

6
00:00:09,138 --> 00:00:11,682
Today its east end is gated off, and has

7
00:00:11,692 --> 00:00:12,693
been for decades.

8
00:00:13,093 --> 00:00:15,441
Legend says a young woman named Elizabeth

9
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:17,654
Wilson was in a car that went off the road

10
00:00:17,664 --> 00:00:21,110
in the 1950s, into a swamp, and never made

11
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:21,532
it home.

12
00:00:22,082 --> 00:00:24,042
People say she still walks the road,

13
00:00:24,052 --> 00:00:25,090
looking for a ride.

14
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,298
And drivers who stop for her say she

15
00:00:27,308 --> 00:00:29,110
vanishes near Ross Cemetery.

16
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:32,226
Others report a dark figure walking the

17
00:00:32,236 --> 00:00:34,709
railroad tracks nearby, sometimes carrying

18
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:35,359
a lantern.

19
00:00:35,909 --> 00:00:38,036
But the Ghost Research Society says it

20
00:00:38,046 --> 00:00:40,516
found no burial record for an Elizabeth

21
00:00:40,526 --> 00:00:42,190
Wilson at Ross Cemetery.

22
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,550
And some say she's still out there,

23
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:45,638
waiting by the road.

24
00:00:46,138 --> 00:00:48,181
Comment your town, and it could be next.

